 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T12:45+08:00",
 "answer": "**No, it is not safe to exercise outdoors in Jurong right now.** \n\nSingapore is currently experiencing an ongoing haze episode, and air quality remains in the **unhealthy to very unhealthy** range. In the western region (including Jurong East and Jurong West), hourly PM2.5 levels remain elevated. \n\n### Current Recommendations:\n* **General Public:** Avoid strenuous or prolonged outdoor physical activity. Workouts should be moved indoors.\n* **Sensitive Groups** (children, the elderly, pregnant women, and those with pre-existing heart or respiratory conditions like asthma): **Strictly remain indoors** and minimize all physical exertion.\n* **Facilities:** National sports agencies have closed outdoor and non-air-conditioned ActiveSG facilities in response to the haze. \n\nIf you must head out briefly, check real-time updates via the [NEA myENV app](https://www.nea.gov.sg/) and consider wearing an N95 mask if exposure is unavoidable.",
